From 8875d88562609d58e66748057cf670bc55fe445d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Safeer <info@safeer.si>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:10:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fall back to IPv4 when the OS has no IPv6 support

On Linux booted with ipv6.disable=1 (and in some containers) creating any
AF_INET6 socket fails with EAFNOSUPPORT. rqbit binds [::] by default for the
TCP listener, the DHT, LSD and the UDP tracker client, so the session does
not start at all:

    error initializing rqbit session
    Caused by:
        0: error starting listeners
        1: error starting TCP listener
        2: error creating socket: Address family not supported by protocol (os error 97)

--ipv4-only does not help either, because the UDP tracker client always
binds [::]:0:

        0: error creating UDP tracker client
        1: error creating UDP socket at [::]:0
        2: error creating socket: Address family not supported by protocol (os error 97)

- Session::new_with_opts probes whether an IPv6 socket can be created. On
  EAFNOSUPPORT it logs a warning and behaves as if ipv4_only was set
  (listener included). If IPv6 is available nothing changes.
- UdpTrackerClient::new takes ipv4_only and binds 0.0.0.0:0 when it is set.
- LocalServiceDiscoveryOptions gets ipv4_only (binds 0.0.0.0:6771).
- rqbit share: the default HTTP API address is 0.0.0.0:0 when IPv4 only.

On a host without IPv6 the existing e2e tests (test_e2e_download_tcp,
test_e2e_download_utp, test_e2e_stream) failed before this change for the
same reason and pass with it. New tests: test_fallback_to_ipv4_only_if_no_ipv6,
test_session_starts_with_default_listen_addr, test_ipv4_only_binds_ipv4.
